# SYNTHETIC. Written from RFC 5321 and RFC 6152. Not a recording:
# phase-0 capture against a real server has not happened yet.
# The message contains octets above 7 bits and the server advertised 8BITMIME,
# so MAIL FROM carries BODY=8BITMIME.

S: 220 smtp.example ESMTP ready
C: EHLO client.example
S: 250-smtp.example Hello
S: 250-8BITMIME
S: 250 AUTH PLAIN
C: AUTH PLAIN AGFkYUBleGFtcGxlLmNvbQBzM2NyM3QtcGFzc3dvcmQ=
S: 235 2.7.0 Authentication successful
C: MAIL FROM:<ada@example.com> BODY=8BITMIME
S: 250 2.1.0 OK
C: RCPT TO:<bob@example.com>
S: 250 2.1.5 OK
C: DATA
S: 354 go ahead
C: café
C: .
S: 250 2.0.0 OK queued
C: QUIT
S: 221 2.0.0 Bye
DONE
